## 🆘 Troubleshooting

### "Pod stuck in Pending"
```bash
kubectl describe pod -n inference -l app=vllm-tinyllama
```
Usually means GPU quota not available. Try a different zone.

### "GPU not available"
Wait longer for driver installation, or check:
```bash
kubectl get nodes -o wide
kubectl describe node | grep -A5 "Capacity:"
```

### "Permission denied"
Make sure RBAC is applied:
```bash
kubectl apply -f rbac/
```

### "Model loading slow"
TinyLlama is small (~2GB). If it takes >10 minutes, check logs:
```bash
kubectl logs -n inference -l app=vllm-tinyllama -f
```

---

## 📝 Quick Reference Commands

```bash
# Check cluster status
gcloud container clusters list

# Check pods
kubectl get pods -n inference

# Check pod logs
kubectl logs -n inference -l app=vllm-tinyllama

# Delete everything and stop billing
gcloud container clusters delete piqc-test --zone=us-central1-a --quiet
```

---

> 💡 **Remember**: Always delete the cluster when done to stop billing!
